<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-SocGen raised at Lehman.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-SocGen raised at Lehman.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale was raised to &quot;outperform&quot; from &quot;neutral&quot; at Lehman Brothers, a research note from analyst Sheil Garrard at the brokerage said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Garrard said she raised her forcast for 1997 net income to 5.075 billion francs from 4.935 billion.</p>
<p>Lehman also upped BNP to &quot;outperform&quot; as part of a review of French bank stocks, saying the whole sector was due a re-rating.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
